---
layout: null
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#- /menus/ once the menus have moved to 88's menu.<domain> pages (menus.md).
    Same stub shape as legacy-redirects.njk, but the destination is absolute:
    EleventyHtmlBasePlugin leaves it alone, and the canonical names it as is.

    An old `/menus/#menu-<scheduleId>` link cannot become a slug here — the
    fragment never reaches the server and the build does not know the mapping
    — so it lands on the menu root, which opens the first menu. Anything that
    still links to one menu should move to menuLink(slug, scheduleId). -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <title>Redirecting…</title>
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ client.urls.menus }}">
    <link rel="canonical" href="{{ client.urls.menus }}">
  </head>
  <body>
    <p>Our menu has moved to <a href="{{ client.urls.menus }}">{{ client.urls.menus }}</a>.</p>
  </body>
</html>
